fontconvert_sdcard.py: kern with OpenType's first-match rule (NOT applied yet)

Today the converter adds up every GPOS 'kern' PairPos subtable and the legacy
'kern' table. OpenType applies only the first subtable of a lookup that
matches a pair (that is how glyph-pair exceptions override class kerning),
and shapers ignore 'kern' when GPOS has kerning. This patch does the same.
Measured at 14 pt it changes 3,973 pairs in Literata Regular and 101 in
SourceSerif4 (e.g. "Vã" -61/16 px -> -23/16 px).

Apply together with the browser side, which already has the same rule behind
an option: convertFamily(ft, { ..., kerning: 'first-match' }).
Verified byte-identical against this patched script with
  node test/file_parity.mjs --kerning first-match --script <patched script>

  git apply tools/ftwasm/patches/fontconvert_sdcard-kerning-first-match.patch

